&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./asonicsignature&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;asonicsignature&quot;&gt;Sonic signatures&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: During a breakfast with a friend, I realized the significance of sound design in our digital interactions as the keyboard clicks from his iPhone reminded me how these auditory cues, often muted in my own life, add intentionality and richness to the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./canakiddrawit&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;canakiddrawit&quot;&gt;Can a kid draw it?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Simplicity in tech design, exemplified by Apple’s products, enhances usability and appeal, but true design excellence lies in balancing accessibility with functionality and innovation, rather than merely adhering to a child-like simplicity as discussed in the text.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./gamer&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;gamer&quot;&gt;The “gamer” aesthetic is beyond awful&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The gaming industry’s design aesthetic, dominated by flashy and superficial elements reminiscent of neon kitsch, suggests a missed opportunity for sophistication in gaming hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./tags/design&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;tags/design&quot;&gt;Other posts on Design&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;internet&quot;&gt;Internet&lt;a role=&quot;anchor&quot; aria-hidden tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; data-no-popover href=&quot;#internet&quot; class=&quot;internal&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;18&quot; height=&quot;18&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; stroke=&quot;currentColor&quot; stroke-width=&quot;2&quot; stroke-linecap=&quot;round&quot; stroke-linejoin=&quot;round&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./sentmyfromiphone&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;sentmyfromiphone&quot;&gt;Sent from my iPhone&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Using the default Mail app on iOS led me to unwittingly send an email with the signature “Envoyé de mon iPhone,” prompting a reflection on how this seemingly innocuous phrase has transformed from a status symbol into a cringe-worthy marker of pretension and digital etiquette.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./dreamsofconvenience&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;dreamsofconvenience&quot;&gt;Dreams of convenience&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: As digital platforms prioritize profit over user experience, the internet feels more suffocating than ever, with personal interactions overshadowed by excessive advertisements and misleading content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./whataboutme&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;whataboutme&quot;&gt;What about me?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The &lt;i&gt;What about me?&lt;/i&gt; effect highlights a cognitive bias where online content must cater to specific needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;./tags/internet&quot; class=&quot;internal alias&quot; data-slug=&quot;tags/internet&quot;&gt;Other posts on the Internet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
